{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <set>\n#include <map>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing lint = long long;\nconst lint MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nlint mod_exp(lint base, lint exp, lint mod) {\n    lint res = 1;\n    base %= mod;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) res = (res * base) % mod;\n        base = (base * base) % mod;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int P, K;\n    cin >> P >> K;\n    \n    vector<int> parent(P + 1);\n    for (int i = 1; i <= P; i++) parent[i] = i;\n    \n    auto find_root = [&](int x) {\n        vector<int> path;\n        while (parent[x] != x) {\n            path.push_back(x);\n            x = parent[x];\n        }\n        for (int node : path) parent[node] = x;\n        return x;\n    };\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i < P; i++) {\n        lint target = (1LL * K * i) % P;\n        if (target == 0) target = P;\n        int root1 = find_root(i);\n        int root2 = find_root((int)target);\n        if (root1 != root2) {\n            parent[root2] = root1;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    set<int> unique_roots;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= P; i++) {\n        unique_roots.insert(find_root(i));\n    }\n    \n    lint answer;\n    if (K == 0) {\n        answer = mod_exp((lint)P, (lint)(P - 1), MOD);\n    } else if (K == 1) {\n        answer = mod_exp((lint)P, (lint)P, MOD);\n    } else {\n        answer = mod_exp((lint)P, (lint)unique_roots.size(), MOD);\n    }\n    \n    cout << answer << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n    static long mod_exp(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long res = 1;\n        base %= mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                res = (res * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int P = scanner.nextInt();\n        int K = scanner.nextInt();\n        \n        int[] parent = new int[P + 1];\n        for (int i = 1; i <= P; i++) {\n            parent[i] = i;\n        }\n        \n        class UnionFind {\n            int[] parent;\n            \n            UnionFind(int[] p) {\n                this.parent = p;\n            }\n            \n            int find_root(int x) {\n                List<Integer> path = new ArrayList<>();\n                while (parent[x] != x) {\n                    path.add(x);\n                    x = parent[x];\n                }\n                for (int node : path) {\n                    parent[node] = x;\n                }\n                return x;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        UnionFind uf = new UnionFind(parent);\n        \n        for (int i = 1; i < P; i++) {\n            long target = (1L * K * i) % P;\n            if (target == 0) {\n                target = P;\n            }\n            int root1 = uf.find_root(i);\n            int root2 = uf.find_root((int)target);\n            if (root1 != root2) {\n                parent[root2] = root1;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        Set<Integer> unique_roots = new HashSet<>();\n        for (int i = 1; i <= P; i++) {\n            unique_roots.add(uf.find_root(i));\n        }\n        \n        long answer;\n        if (K == 0) {\n            answer = mod_exp((long)P, (long)(P - 1), MOD);\n        } else if (K == 1) {\n            answer = mod_exp((long)P, (long)P, MOD);\n        } else {\n            answer = mod_exp((long)P, (long)unique_roots.size(), MOD);\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(answer);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012575789878610522, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -8.439661905867979e-05, -3.313963316031732e-05, -0.004086715634912252, -0.5231516361236572, -7.986990567587782e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -5.149708886165172e-05, -0.0002965487365145236, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.055314287543296814, -0.00044383687782101333, -9.297892393078655e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.4781842764932662e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0008924792055040598, -0.01603446528315544, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.0028067738749086857, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -7.629365427419543e-06, -0.31348830461502075, -4.0649541915627196e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -7.033323527139146e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -6.747018051100895e-05, -3.099436753473128e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -3.099436753473128e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -4.76